# Laravel API Rules

- Keep controllers thin; orchestration only.
- Place business logic in dedicated services/actions.
- Use repository pattern only when it adds clear value.
- Validate inputs with Form Requests and explicit rules.
- Return responses through API Resources/Transformers.
- Move heavy operations to queued jobs.
- Enforce authorization with policies and permissions.
- Keep migrations clean, reversible, and consistent.
- Never place business logic in controllers.
- Use Laravel translation keys in `file.key` format only, with flat keys (for example `messages.order_created`).
- Follow domain architecture and coding baseline in `docs/guides/laravel-backend-bible.md`.
